{title: I Know My God Can Do It}
{key: Bb}

{comment: Verse 1}
[Bb]Three Hebrew boys were thrown into the fire,
Because before the [C]King they [F]would not bow;
But they [Bb]said, "Listen King, let it be known,
We serve the living God, [F]we're not alone."

{comment: Chorus}
Well, [Bb]I know my God can do it,
To Him there's nothing to it.
I know He'll see you through it,
[C]Sweet victo[F]ry.
Well, [Bb]even when the storms are raging,
He is the Rock of Ages,
I know that He is able, mighty is He.

{comment: Verse 2}
[Bb]They marched around the walls of Jericho.
They knew that they would [C]fall, [F]God told them so.
Just like [Bb]He worked for them, He's working now,
My God will never change, [F]He has great powers.
